WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
How many children can share 2 rotis, if each gets a quarter?

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Bilal has 2 rotis. Each child gets a quarter of a roti.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Cut each roti into quarters. One roti makes 4 quarters.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Count the quarters: 2 rotis make 8 quarters. So 8 children can eat.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Dividing by a quarter gives the same answer as multiplying by 4.

6
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Dividing by 1/4 asks: how many quarters fit? That is why the answer is bigger than 2.

